{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1576 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0a17d5dcd6a70059aad2c09309a1374a34b093aca82b4c0689f05c312e08e507" :edb/db-before-t 1575 :edb/db-after-t 1576 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534888 50 #inst "2026-10-08T10:09:50.584Z" 13194139534888 true] [17592186114987 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\n\t\\begin{array}{rl} & x + 5 y + z = 2 \\\\  & x + 5 y + 2 z = 5.\\end{array}\n\t\\right.\n$$\n\n.\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534888 false] [17592186114987 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/a50d551e5d8abe8d9ae48778b195c382bbbf96f6fc5083c41b67642e99deffda.png)\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534888 true] [17592186114987 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\n\t\\left[\n\t\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 5\\end{array}\n\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rlrl}M & \\sim \\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & := {R}_{2} + ( - 1 ) {R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim \\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & := {R}_{1} + ( - 1 ) {R}_{2} \\\\  & \\sim \\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 5 & 0 & - 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{array}$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\\left\\{\n\\begin{array}{rl} & x + 5 y = - 1 \\\\  & z = 3.\\end{array}\n\\right.$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $z$, and we have one free variable, $y$. That means we need to find $x$ and $z$ in terms of $y$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}x = - 1 - 5 y \\\\ y = y \\\\ z = 3 ,\\end{array} \\right.$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 - 5y \\\\ y \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}, y \\in  (- \\infty , \\infty )\n$$" 13194139534888 false] [17592186114987 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/48c423256fbdc0d7e4f6ff716fb449efe6f98bdf57ba90353bcced930ea4ed17.png)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/81b7626ac30b06c5eeb10be274dd93476a86dce5fe3053722d96e16b78d7f165.png)\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $z,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $z$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-5y \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-5y \\\\ y \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186114988 1100 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}2 x - 2 y = 1 , \\\\ 4 x + k y = - 3\\end{array} \\right.\n$$" 13194139534888 false] [17592186114988 1100 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y=1, \\\\ 4x+ky=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186114988 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/a115d3da691619918bf92d914acdfdd95088e9a141a82ca3fe3230fa7fbb8172.png)\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/cfea36ae2b5cb5d8715480c1e0ee0b5ba06cf39d0c2032eb6e9b9078bf8c5bde.png)\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186114988 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$M=\n\t\\left[\n\t\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & - 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & - 3\\end{array}\n\\right].$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rlrl}M & = \\left[ \\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & - 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & - 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & := {R}_{2} - 2 {R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim \\left[ \\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & - 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k + 4 & - 5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{array}$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\\left\\{\n\\begin{array}{rl} & 2 x - 2 y = 1 \\\\  & ( k + 4 ) y = - 5.\\end{array}\n\\right.$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4$, then the second equation is $0=-5$, which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4$." 13194139534888 false] [17592186115041 1100 "Given the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\n\t\\begin{array}{rl} & 2 x - 3 y = 4 \\\\  & - 4 x + 6 y = - 8 ,\\end{array}\n\t\\right.\n$$\n\n,\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The system is consistent dependent\n2. The system has no solution\n3. The system is consistent independent" 13194139534888 false] [17592186115041 1100 "Given the system\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/5f1aaf29a3dd8b7ea2c4f7104d532f7b56f32a23ccebbcfa0d1bfe86c772cc5f.png)\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n\n- The system has no solution\n\n- The system is consistent independent" 13194139534888 true] [17592186115041 1145 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\n\t\\left[\n\t\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & - 3 & 4 \\\\ - 4 & 6 & - 8\\end{array}\n\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rlrl}M & = \\left[ \\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & - 3 & 4 \\\\ - 4 & 6 & - 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & := {R}_{2} + 2 {R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim \\left[ \\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & - 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{array}$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\\left\\{\n\t\\begin{array}{rl} & 2 x - 3 y = 4 \\\\  & 0 x + 0 y = 0.\\end{array}\n\t\\right.$$\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation\n\n$$\n0x+0y=0\n$$\n\nwe can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x -3y= 4\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x$, and we have a free variable $y$. That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$.\n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." 13194139534888 false] [17592186115041 1145 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/6171d242b0a3887802f629de79cb952d47711a581e88db2d9304a5db356dfb62.png)\n\nUsing Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/80aff0fd62e3e1aeed17017c864d8d0b875b556ce1a29a89e6c61e632bf9c733.png)\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x -3y= 4\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x,$ and we have a free variable $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." 13194139534888 true] [17592186115161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317551 13194139534888 true] [17592186115161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317558 13194139534888 true] [17592186115161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317607 13194139534888 true] [17592186115161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317614 13194139534888 true] [17592186115161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317628 13194139534888 true] [17592186115162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317586 13194139534888 true] [17592186115162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317593 13194139534888 true] [17592186115162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317600 13194139534888 true] [17592186115162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317635 13194139534888 true] [17592186115219 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317565 13194139534888 true] [17592186115219 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317572 13194139534888 true] [17592186115219 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317579 13194139534888 true] [17592186115219 1020 #edb/ref 17592186317621 13194139534888 true] [17592186115672 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534888 true] [17592186115672 1100 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{rl} & 3 x + 4 y = 12 \\\\  & x + k y = 4\\end{array} \\right.\n$$" 13194139534888 false] [17592186115672 1100 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+4y=12 \\\\  & x+ky=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186115672 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 12 \\\\ 1 & k & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 12 \\\\ 1 & k & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4-3k & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+ky=4 \\\\  & (4-3k)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=\\frac{4}{3},$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+ky=4.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=\\frac{4}{3}.$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186115743 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534888 true] [17592186115743 1100 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{rl} & x - 3 y + z = 0 \\\\  & - 4 x + 6 y = 2\\end{array} \\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The system is consistent dependent\n2. The system has no solution\n3. The system is consistent independent" 13194139534888 false] [17592186115743 1100 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=0 \\\\  & -4x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent" 13194139534888 true] [17592186115743 1145 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." 13194139534888 true] [17592186317551 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317552 13194139534888 true] [17592186317551 1089 "q-131712" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317551 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534888 true] [17592186317551 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+8y=-6 \\\\  & -4x-16y=12 \\\\  & 6x+24y=-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534888 true] [17592186317551 1113 #uuid "b0feb9ee-8e97-5292-aff6-05655689f05b" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317551 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$  in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-4y-3 \\\\ y=y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4y-3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317553 13194139534888 true] [17592186317552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317554 13194139534888 true] [17592186317552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317555 13194139534888 true] [17592186317552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317556 13194139534888 true] [17592186317552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317557 13194139534888 true] [17592186317552 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534888 true] [17592186317552 1041 "selection" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317552 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317554 13194139534888 true] [17592186317552 1110 #uuid "c94cbe09-bdb3-5177-b965-eab79df51cb6" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317553 1034 "No solution" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317553 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317553 1111 #uuid "56836203-c4be-53e9-b541-53a7bedc87b1" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317554 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-4y-3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317554 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317554 1111 #uuid "abf4b289-daed-5182-a993-644d739be96c" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317555 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}4y+3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317555 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317555 1111 #uuid "c4f6f0f7-d6ab-508e-9ece-17d869f2c1cc" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317556 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}4y-3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317556 1111 #uuid "922b9afb-4edf-5afd-926d-9a8590705ddd" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317557 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}3-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317557 1111 #uuid "ee8a01d4-8cb1-5cd3-a55e-21515404bc40" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317558 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317559 13194139534888 true] [17592186317558 1089 "q-131717" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317558 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534888 true] [17592186317558 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534888 true] [17592186317558 1113 #uuid "ea253a83-404b-5d27-8e99-ab1346327cc6" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317558 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-5{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}={x}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ 1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317560 13194139534888 true] [17592186317559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317561 13194139534888 true] [17592186317559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317562 13194139534888 true] [17592186317559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317563 13194139534888 true] [17592186317559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317564 13194139534888 true] [17592186317559 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534888 true] [17592186317559 1041 "selection" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317559 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317564 13194139534888 true] [17592186317559 1110 #uuid "0efdee88-6a7c-5974-993d-2ab3cf0ff497" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317560 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}4-5{x}_{3} \\\\ 1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317560 1111 #uuid "f763111a-5af4-5488-a929-0020e0aeba2a" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317561 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ 2{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317561 1111 #uuid "59bbb71e-60d8-5eae-8d64-214b3d7c235e" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317562 1034 "No solution" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317562 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317562 1111 #uuid "18dc88f8-bcb4-52ae-adfb-a82167f7d74d" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317563 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{3}+4 \\\\ 2{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317563 1111 #uuid "d6d2bc07-7dc8-55a2-81a6-b1489f131d1b" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317564 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ 1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317564 1111 #uuid "0c30fead-4a73-5022-9e9a-21dd0b0638a5" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317565 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317566 13194139534888 true] [17592186317565 1089 "q-131719" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317565 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534888 true] [17592186317565 1100 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=-1 \\\\  & 2x+8y=-2 \\\\  & -3x-12y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is inconsistent\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has a unique solution" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317565 1113 #uuid "85139672-fc12-5f19-974e-cd9c9c3f59d6" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317565 1145 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we can find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." 13194139534888 true] [17592186317566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317567 13194139534888 true] [17592186317566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317568 13194139534888 true] [17592186317566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317569 13194139534888 true] [17592186317566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317570 13194139534888 true] [17592186317566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317571 13194139534888 true] [17592186317566 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534888 true] [17592186317566 1041 "selection" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317566 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317571 13194139534888 true] [17592186317566 1110 #uuid "33fce12e-12f7-5945-a801-72dea6bcf2e8" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317567 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317567 1111 #uuid "f81946b8-0e51-5d2c-a843-bc2231e1d145" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317568 1034 "I only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317568 1111 #uuid "4e841753-e6ff-5ea7-b26f-6d9575329fa9" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317569 1034 "III only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317569 1111 #uuid "33e69ce1-6954-5201-8c9c-5e864e29e461" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317570 1034 "None" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317570 1111 #uuid "2e3ae4ee-b56e-5f4e-aae8-59dacc65408d" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317571 1034 "II only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317571 1111 #uuid "a5ba308b-dbba-56f5-baa5-466e5aeb13fe" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317572 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317573 13194139534888 true] [17592186317572 1089 "q-131722" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317572 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534888 true] [17592186317572 1100 "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x-3y=6 \\\\  & -2x+y=-3 \\\\  & 4x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system has no solution" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317572 1113 #uuid "4890e1ff-ed9a-5558-acd1-bcef01439e04" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317572 1145 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=-1$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=1.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." 13194139534888 true] [17592186317573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317574 13194139534888 true] [17592186317573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317575 13194139534888 true] [17592186317573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317576 13194139534888 true] [17592186317573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317577 13194139534888 true] [17592186317573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317578 13194139534888 true] [17592186317573 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534888 true] [17592186317573 1041 "selection" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317573 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317578 13194139534888 true] [17592186317573 1110 #uuid "b05a5f36-6352-563f-aae4-29464953bae5" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317574 1034 "I only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317574 1111 #uuid "908a019e-8258-54e1-a3e6-de86654a1050" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317575 1034 "III only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317575 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317575 1111 #uuid "ea552307-27bc-5f39-aeb6-7cbb6673ebb6" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317576 1034 "None" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317576 1111 #uuid "1e6537cf-4f5d-52e6-94e3-f493b4f11925" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317577 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317577 1111 #uuid "d27cbb7b-ab8d-5431-b448-c300eaa43995" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317578 1034 "II only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317578 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317578 1111 #uuid "4b8dd03f-0f8a-5866-a7eb-663a28f92dd6" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317579 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317580 13194139534888 true] [17592186317579 1089 "q-131724" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317579 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534888 true] [17592186317579 1100 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y=2 \\\\  & -3x-4y=3 \\\\  & 2x-4y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has a unique solution\n- The system is inconsistent" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317579 1113 #uuid "e93f981b-b1bd-511a-87f1-b614c74c85ee" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317579 1145 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-5,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." 13194139534888 true] [17592186317580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317581 13194139534888 true] [17592186317580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317582 13194139534888 true] [17592186317580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317583 13194139534888 true] [17592186317580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317584 13194139534888 true] [17592186317580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317585 13194139534888 true] [17592186317580 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534888 true] [17592186317580 1041 "selection" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317580 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317582 13194139534888 true] [17592186317580 1110 #uuid "43dbb445-b54a-5c1b-aa3d-7705c663ae63" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317581 1034 "I only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317581 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317581 1111 #uuid "1c0b9397-ce4f-5728-b49f-219395f94aac" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317582 1034 "III only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317582 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317582 1111 #uuid "b51758dc-7f53-57bf-92cf-0283d4a01944" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317583 1034 "None" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317583 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317583 1111 #uuid "e6b7640a-48ae-5763-9b0d-2ea31e3bb516" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317584 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317584 1111 #uuid "78a929b9-0473-539f-beb7-2bbefc400063" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317585 1034 "II only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317585 1111 #uuid "9bd15515-5743-5020-981f-7c4b2f450897" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317586 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317587 13194139534888 true] [17592186317586 1089 "q-131727" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317586 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534888 true] [17592186317586 1100 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y=-1 \\\\  & 4x+3ky=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317586 1113 #uuid "d47e9f79-9224-5415-86c6-0753b047d174" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317586 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3k & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3k & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3k+12 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=-1 \\\\ (3k+12)y=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=7,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317588 13194139534888 true] [17592186317587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317589 13194139534888 true] [17592186317587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317590 13194139534888 true] [17592186317587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317591 13194139534888 true] [17592186317587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317592 13194139534888 true] [17592186317587 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534888 true] [17592186317587 1041 "selection" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317587 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317592 13194139534888 true] [17592186317587 1110 #uuid "47e2311e-69cb-5a3f-99ce-e1179d238593" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317588 1034 "k=-12" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317588 