 the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534888 true] [17592186317614 1113 #uuid "013e11bb-39c0-595b-a244-03847638286f" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317614 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=0 \\\\  & y-z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ y=z-1 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317616 13194139534888 true] [17592186317615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317617 13194139534888 true] [17592186317615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317618 13194139534888 true] [17592186317615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317619 13194139534888 true] [17592186317615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317620 13194139534888 true] [17592186317615 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534888 true] [17592186317615 1041 "selection" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317615 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317619 13194139534888 true] [17592186317615 1110 #uuid "47bbcdd9-b23e-52e8-94f0-96d651969d9b" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317616 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}2-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317616 1111 #uuid "c8fb9412-eb4b-5fc7-a668-6254be1176b5" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317617 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317617 1111 #uuid "180aa355-38f3-5bc4-a98d-6089535eaac0" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317618 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-z \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317618 1111 #uuid "43677cd0-73bf-5272-95a1-c7d210e1257c" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317619 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317619 1111 #uuid "3a715954-196e-5121-9eb2-a071e7214ff8" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317620 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317620 1111 #uuid "118b2c2b-be06-5fce-b85e-7beb4cab4232" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317621 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317622 13194139534888 true] [17592186317621 1089 "q-42020" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317621 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534888 true] [17592186317621 1100 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y=-1 \\\\  & 3x+y=3 \\\\  & -2x+y=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system has a unique solution\n- The system is inconsistent" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317621 1113 #uuid "1a930b2a-2578-5145-8e40-06b6cab16ba9" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317621 1145 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=2,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." 13194139534888 true] [17592186317622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317623 13194139534888 true] [17592186317622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317624 13194139534888 true] [17592186317622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317625 13194139534888 true] [17592186317622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317626 13194139534888 true] [17592186317622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317627 13194139534888 true] [17592186317622 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534888 true] [17592186317622 1041 "selection" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317622 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317625 13194139534888 true] [17592186317622 1110 #uuid "daf102e0-7cc7-5eb1-8770-e5338389ece2" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317623 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317623 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317623 1111 #uuid "9eaa3d19-5e97-5969-be15-6d2f7e90d195" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317624 1034 "I only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317624 1111 #uuid "233786e0-6b57-514b-998e-fa7d6da6c104" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317625 1034 "III only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317625 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317625 1111 #uuid "14e5e29b-adbe-5916-bfa3-e152421f2417" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317626 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317626 1111 #uuid "f6ff5d69-7707-5b49-863c-a61832e1f51b" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317627 1034 "II only" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534888 true] [17592186317627 1111 #uuid "b8035881-063f-5748-82a7-e8e17c4d482c" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317628 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317629 13194139534888 true] [17592186317628 1089 "q-42041" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317628 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534888 true] [17592186317628 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-4z=2 \\\\ 4x+y-5z=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139534888 true] [17592186317628 1113 #uuid "09fe1174-4802-515f-8d41-d02fb865fb55" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317628 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2z=1 \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+2z \\\\ y=-3z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+2z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317630 13194139534888 true] [17592186317629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317631 13194139534888 true] [17592186317629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317632 13194139534888 true] [17592186317629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317633 13194139534888 true] [17592186317629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317634 13194139534888 true] [17592186317629 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534888 true] [17592186317629 1041 "selection" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317629 1104 #edb/ref 17592186317631 13194139534888 true] [17592186317629 1110 #uuid "cc7d8608-6cac-5579-9b7d-8a78b7ebbee6" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317630 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}2+4z \\\\ 1-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317630 1111 #uuid "a74658ab-6621-565d-8a89-7358301574eb" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317631 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1+2z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317631 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317631 1111 #uuid "192b6da6-515a-5d39-94fe-459d8d85fff9" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317632 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-2z \\\\ 4z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317632 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317632 1111 #uuid "d956ce98-8354-52ea-b7e2-6f47d9302574" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317633 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}2+4z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317633 1111 #uuid "289b5e1b-d5de-5cd8-a853-a1325eb3ba0d" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317634 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1+4z \\\\ 3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317634 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534888 true] [17592186317634 1111 #uuid "41109a43-3c87-59ca-bcc7-229b8a8eb449" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317635 1017 #edb/ref 17592186317636 13194139534888 true] [17592186317635 1089 "q-74646" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317635 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534888 true] [17592186317635 1100 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=2 \\\\  & 2x+(k+1)y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317635 1113 #uuid "d0469220-01c3-5e98-b2ee-ca1c1a254981" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317635 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & k-7 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=2 \\\\ (k-7)y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=7,$ then the second equation is $0=-1,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=7.$" 13194139534888 true] [17592186317636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317637 13194139534888 true] [17592186317636 1000 #edb/ref 17592186317638 13194139534888 true] [1759218631763